A||N||9||chris6878||Plug Wires...  ?||||9||
Z||000000||chris6878||03-23-2000||01:56 AM||||I pulled my car into the driveway tonight... and was curious and popped the hood...    i noticed my plug wires  arching everywhere...  a least 10 different places...    the wires arent but about a month or 2 old..      should i get better wires that can stand the heat...?   any suggestions?||||reg||9
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-23-2000||02:26 AM||||Accel 300+ had them on for about 8 months, no problems they hold up to the heat really well and they are or 8.8mm spiral core. And they look good!!! about $65.00 a set (Custom Fit)||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierospeeder||03-23-2000||03:23 AM||||i would also get accel, mine also arced when i used the store brand wires.  My car would stumble during acceleration and it would be really bad when it rained.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||WisconsinGT||03-23-2000||04:05 AM||||I gotta say that the SplitFire wires I have on my car sure do work well. They cost around $50.00. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||03-23-2000||08:45 AM||||I have had the Accel wires and the Jacobs Electronics wires. The Jacobs are far better by a good margin and cost about the same. Got mine directly from Jacobs and cost me $60 + s/h. They came with markers and a nice dividers. You can really feel the difference with this wires. I strongly recomend them. Also they have a lifetime warranty. Only problem for some is that they are blue in color. But I preffer performance better than looks...||||reg||12
Z||000005||theogre||03-23-2000||07:46 PM||||I've got 20Kmiles on a set of Borg Warner helical core wires. no problems. And DIS motors are really crabby about wires..... If they are bad you know quick.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||03-24-2000||01:20 AM||||I went into the junkyard today looking for a fuel line for my stationwagon but couldn't find any good ones.  Instead i spotted 4 fieros, 3 are 2.5l and 1 i dont know, the engine lid was locked.  <BR>But i was looking for some parts like an extra windshield pump, got it, and an egr valve rubber hose.  While looking through the car, i found a close to new 8.8 ,i believe, spark plug wires,gray color, the 2nd time i found pretty close to new, wires in a fiero at a junk yard.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||03-24-2000||02:55 PM||||Yep... When a car starts running bad, replacing the wires is about the limit of a lot of peoples ability. If it's and older car and that doesn't do the trick, often it is off to the boneyard!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ROB MAC||03-24-2000||03:40 PM||||Are the wires crisscrossing or running parrallel . Parrallel can cause arching in some cases||||reg||1
Z||000009||chris6878||03-24-2000||07:29 PM||||they are crossing... just ever which way...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">        this is on a v6 too... the wires arent arcing each other..    they are arcing against the metal things around them.. like the plentum, and so on...       i will probally just go for a set that can stand the heat...      thanks for the replies..  <P>chris||||reg||1
